    "linkedin:2aa7dfec503e85c55672ed1f": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Web Developer (Django/Python)",
        "company": "Sundayy",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4469137654",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": false,
        "description": "**About The Company**\n National Journal is a premier research and insights organization dedicated to providing comprehensive and accurate information to government and business leaders in Washington, D.C. With a history spanning nearly 50 years, it has established itself as one of the most trusted media brands in the region. The company specializes in government affairs, political research, and journalism, offering in\\-depth analysis, data, and tools to help its audience navigate the complex landscape of Washington politics and policy. National Journal's mission is to empower its members with the intelligence, insights, and connections necessary to make informed decisions, save time, and achieve success in their respective fields.\n   \n\n  \n\n The organization prides itself on a culture of intellectual rigor, innovation, and service. Its digital platform is a cornerstone of its offerings, featuring a rich set of election data, demographic information, government directories, event listings, and editorial content. The platform is designed to be user\\-centric, providing easy access to critical resources through modern, efficient, and innovative tools developed with cutting\\-edge technologies.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n National Journal is seeking a mid\\-level Django/Python Web Developer to join our dynamic digital team. This full\\-time role is pivotal in developing, maintaining, and enhancing web\\-based tools and platforms that serve our Washington, D.C., audience of government affairs professionals, policy advocates, and political analysts. The successful candidate will work on building robust, scalable, and user\\-friendly digital solutions that facilitate access to election data, policy resources, and analytical tools.\n   \n\n  \n\n This role involves collaborating with cross\\-functional teams to support existing services, develop new features, and improve internal systems such as Ada, our custom content management system. The developer will contribute to a fast\\-paced environment with frequent release cycles, utilizing modern development practices, including AI\\-assisted coding workflows and continuous integration. The position offers flexibility with full\\-time telework or remote arrangements, with options for in\\-person work in Washington, D.C., for local candidates.\n   \n\n  \n\n The ideal candidate will bring a passion for politics and elections, a keen eye for quality, and a desire to leverage technology to make a tangible impact on political research and journalism. They should be eager to learn new tools and frameworks, participate in team discussions about best practices, and contribute to a collaborative, innovative work culture.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n* At least 1 year of professional web development experience using Python and Django\n* Proficiency in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, with experience in front\\-end frameworks a plus\n* Strong understanding of Git version control\n* Experience with LLM\\-based coding assistants such as Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor\n* Knowledge of database management systems like PostgreSQL and MySQL\n* Familiarity with APIs and data integration from internal and third\\-party sources\n* Experience with agile development methodologies and tools\n* Ability to work effectively in a remote or hybrid environment\n* Interest or experience in government, elections, or political data is highly desirable\n* Excellent communication and collaboration skills\n* Demonstrated ability to manage medium to large projects under deadlines\n\n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Design, develop, test, and deploy web\\-based tools and applications primarily using Django and Python\n* Support and enhance the digital platform providing election data, demographic info, and analytical resources\n* Maintain and update large datasets stored in PostgreSQL, MySQL, and via APIs\n* Improve and support Ada, the internal content management system\n* Create automation tools for internal teams, incorporating AI where appropriate\n* Participate in code reviews, write automated tests, and ensure code quality and performance\n* Collaborate with product managers and stakeholders to prioritize features and deliverables\n* Stay informed about emerging trends in software development, AI, and data management\n* Contribute to team discussions on architecture, best practices, and workflow improvements\n\n\n**Benefits**\n* Competitive annual salary starting at $100,000, commensurate with experience\n* Flexible full\\-time telework/remote work arrangements within eligible states\n* Option for in\\-person work in Washington, D.C., three days a week\n* Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance plans\n* Generous paid time off and holidays\n* Professional development opportunities and access to cutting\\-edge tools and technologies\n* A collaborative and inclusive work environment that values diversity and innovation\n\n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n National Journal is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We do not discriminate against applicants or employees based on race, color, religion, sex (including gender identity and sexual orientation), national origin, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other legally protected status. We encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply and consider joining our team.",
        "job_id": "linkedin:2aa7dfec503e85c55672ed1f",
